From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iván Ruiz <iruizl2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:48:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Drop the battery and
 AC nodes on the Surface Pro 11

On the Snapdragon Surface Pro 11, the battery and the charger are
already exposed by qcom_battmgr through pmic_glink (qcom-battmgr-bat,
qcom-battmgr-ac), which also carries the charge control thresholds.
The Surface Aggregator nodes add a second battery and mains supply for
the same hardware (BAT1, ADP1), and UPower sums the two batteries: its
display device reports twice the capacity (93 Wh instead of 46.5 Wh)
and twice the power draw.

The Surface Laptop 7 and the Surface Pro 12in, the other Snapdragon
Surface devices, do not register these nodes either. Drop
them from the Surface Pro 11 group too.

Fixes: c4a069095395 ("platform/surface: aggregator_registry: Add Surface Pro 11 (QCOM)")
Assisted-by: LLM

---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
index 2d1df5b..c33699a 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -419,8 +419,6 @@ static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp9_5g[] = {
 static const struct software_node *ssam_node_group_sp11[] = {
 	&ssam_node_root,
 	&ssam_node_hub_kip,
-	&ssam_node_bat_ac,
-	&ssam_node_bat_main,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_perf_profile_with_fan,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_sensors,
 	&ssam_node_fan_speed,
-- 
